{"id":"data-collecting-cleaning","title":"Data science: collecting and cleaning data","subject":"Data science","label":"Data science","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":182,"duration":182.2,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":478,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"Garbage in","start":0,"end":12.025},{"id":"explain","title":"Collecting data","start":12.025,"end":47.065},{"id":"explain2","title":"Cleaning data","start":47.065,"end":90.265},{"id":"example","title":"Worked example","start":90.265,"end":122.785},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":122.785,"end":132.235},{"id":"answer","title":"Answer","start":132.235,"end":137.385},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":137.385,"end":159.525},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap","start":159.525,"end":182.2}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.05,"text":"Have you ever seen a survey give a confident answer that felt wrong?","w":[0.56,0.72,0.9,1.12,1.36,1.5,1.92,2.12,2.2,2.78,3.14,3.36,3.62]},{"s":0,"a":4.5,"b":11.6,"text":"I'm Kora. Today we look at data science. We ask how to collect data fairly, and how to clean it before you trust any result.","w":[4.6,4.78,5.62,5.92,6.04,6.24,6.34,6.62,7.46,7.68,7.9,8.08,8.18,8.48,8.76,9.4,9.54,9.7,9.84,10.14,10.24,10.52,10.66,10.98,11.18]},{"s":1,"a":12.45,"b":18.77,"text":"Start with the saying. Garbage in, garbage out. An analysis is only as good as its data.","w":[12.58,12.86,13.02,13.16,13.96,14.4,14.96,15.42,16.16,16.3,17.1,17.36,17.66,17.8,18.12,18.26,18.42]},{"s":1,"a":19.07,"b":24.79,"text":"The population is everyone or everything you want to know about. A sample is the part you actually measure.","w":[19.08,19.2,19.88,20.12,20.72,21,21.36,21.5,21.68,21.78,21.96,22.8,22.94,23.36,23.46,23.58,23.82,24.06,24.44]},{"s":1,"a":25.09,"b":31.02,"text":"A good sample is representative. Choosing people at random is the best protection against bias.","w":[25.16,25.28,25.54,26.1,26.26,27.48,27.88,28.24,28.36,28.92,29.02,29.18,29.46,30.1,30.48]},{"s":1,"a":31.32,"b":34.55,"text":"A biased sample gives wrong answers however big it is.","w":[31.42,31.52,32.02,32.46,32.74,33.12,33.48,33.92,34.12,34.28]},{"s":1,"a":34.85,"b":38.42,"text":"Ask only people at a football match about the nation's favourite sport.","w":[34.98,35.34,35.56,35.88,35.98,36.06,36.48,36.82,37.04,37.18,37.62,38]},{"s":1,"a":38.72,"b":40.56,"text":"You will not learn the nation's view.","w":[38.76,38.88,39.1,39.34,39.62,39.74,40.18]},{"s":1,"a":40.86,"b":46.64,"text":"Larger random samples give steadier results. Ask clear, neutral questions, and record units.","w":[40.92,41.38,41.8,42.22,42.44,42.84,43.84,44.18,44.5,44.86,45.6,45.74,46.18]},{"s":2,"a":47.49,"b":51.01,"text":"Cleaning is where data scientists spend a large share of their time.","w":[47.56,47.98,48.1,48.3,48.6,49.34,49.64,49.74,50.14,50.4,50.5,50.66]},{"s":2,"a":51.31,"b":58.75,"text":"First, find missing values. Then decide. Leave them out, or fill them in carefully, and say what you did.","w":[51.4,51.98,52.32,52.68,53.74,53.96,55.06,55.3,55.52,56.12,56.3,56.52,56.68,56.84,57.8,57.98,58.2,58.36,58.52]},{"s":2,"a":59.05,"b":62.77,"text":"Next, remove duplicates, where the same record was entered twice.","w":[59.14,59.62,60.04,60.68,60.88,61.08,61.38,61.7,61.94,62.26]},{"s":2,"a":63.07,"b":70.84,"text":"Fix inconsistent formats and spellings. Lagos, lagos with a small l, and LAGOS in capitals are one city.","w":[63.08,63.46,64.12,64.62,64.78,65.94,67.02,67.5,67.7,67.78,68.32,68.74,68.9,69.4,69.54,70.12,70.38,70.56]},{"s":2,"a":71.14,"b":76.37,"text":"Dates may be written in different orders. Units may be mixed, such as metres and centimetres.","w":[71.16,71.5,71.64,71.78,72.06,72.16,72.54,73.38,73.74,73.92,74.08,74.68,74.92,75.1,75.56,75.7]},{"s":2,"a":76.67,"b":80.61,"text":"Look for impossible values and typing errors, like an age of two hundred.","w":[76.74,76.98,77.16,77.78,78.28,78.4,78.82,79.46,79.64,79.8,80,80.1,80.3]},{"s":2,"a":80.91,"b":85.61,"text":"For outliers, check whether a strange value is a mistake or real before removing it.","w":[80.94,81.2,81.82,82.08,82.38,82.46,82.84,83.24,83.36,83.42,84.1,84.28,84.64,84.98,85.4]},{"s":2,"a":85.91,"b":89.84,"text":"Keep the original file untouched, and write down every change.","w":[85.94,86.24,86.38,86.86,87.36,88.36,88.5,88.74,89.1,89.34]},{"s":3,"a":90.69,"b":92.99,"text":"Here is a survey table with six rows.","w":[90.74,91.02,91.14,91.24,91.62,91.98,92.22,92.52]},{"s":3,"a":93.29,"b":98.02,"text":"One row is a duplicate, so remove it, because the same record was entered twice.","w":[93.44,93.64,94,94.12,94.2,95,95.22,95.56,95.96,96.24,96.4,96.74,97.04,97.24,97.52]},{"s":3,"a":98.32,"b":104.04,"text":"One age is missing, so either leave that row out or fill it carefully, and state your choice.","w":[98.48,98.7,98.92,99.04,99.88,100.1,100.36,100.62,100.84,101.1,101.66,101.8,102.02,102.1,102.92,103.08,103.34,103.54]},{"s":3,"a":104.34,"b":110.43,"text":"The city appears as Lagos, lagos and LAGOS, so make them one spelling, because they mean one city.","w":[104.36,104.52,104.8,105.2,105.36,105.94,106.48,106.62,107.52,107.72,107.92,108.14,108.3,109.06,109.38,109.56,109.92,110.14]},{"s":3,"a":110.73,"b":118.19,"text":"One height is one hundred and seventy among heights like one point seven, so convert it to one point seven metres, because the units are mixed.","w":[110.92,111.1,111.42,111.66,111.84,112.16,112.34,112.76,113.06,113.38,113.66,113.8,114.06,114.7,114.88,115.26,115.36,115.56,115.7,115.96,116.22,116.92,117.22,117.4,117.68,117.82]},{"s":3,"a":118.49,"b":122.36,"text":"Keep the original file untouched, and write down every change you made.","w":[118.5,118.74,118.9,119.32,119.72,120.52,120.66,120.92,121.3,121.6,121.94,122.08]},{"s":4,"a":123.21,"b":129.2,"text":"Quick check. A survey about internet use is carried out only online. What is wrong with the sample?","w":[123.26,123.52,124.32,124.44,124.86,125.18,125.64,125.9,126.04,126.4,126.64,126.94,127.88,128.08,128.2,128.5,128.64,128.76]},{"s":4,"a":129.65,"b":131.81,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[129.68,130,130.26,130.38,130.68,131.34,131.52]},{"s":5,"a":132.66,"b":136.96,"text":"It leaves out people who are rarely or never online, so it is biased.","w":[132.72,132.84,133.18,133.36,133.72,133.9,134.08,134.62,134.78,135.18,135.96,136.12,136.24,136.36]},{"s":6,"a":137.81,"b":144.69,"text":"Three mistakes to avoid. Mistake one. Analysing before looking at the raw data. Always inspect it first.","w":[137.84,138.16,138.62,138.76,139.56,140.04,140.8,141.38,141.7,141.98,142.08,142.24,142.48,143.36,143.74,144.14,144.26]},{"s":6,"a":144.99,"b":153,"text":"Mistake two. Deleting outliers without checking, or filling missing values with guesses and not saying so. Check and record.","w":[145.06,145.48,146.26,146.78,147.28,147.6,148.38,148.56,148.9,149.22,149.58,149.74,150.34,150.48,150.7,151.04,151.88,152.48,152.6]},{"s":6,"a":153.3,"b":159.1,"text":"Mistake three. Thinking a big sample cannot be biased. Size does not remove bias.","w":[153.4,153.78,154.52,154.86,154.96,155.24,155.68,156.1,156.26,157.22,157.62,157.88,158.12,158.54]},{"s":7,"a":159.95,"b":164.85,"text":"Recap. Collect a representative random sample, and ask clear neutral questions.","w":[160.02,160.9,161.24,161.32,161.9,162.28,163.04,163.22,163.5,163.9,164.24]},{"s":7,"a":165.15,"b":171.93,"text":"Clean by finding missing values, duplicates, inconsistent formats, impossible values and outliers.","w":[165.2,165.56,165.76,166.14,166.46,167.3,168.28,168.94,169.94,170.54,171.1,171.28]},{"s":7,"a":172.23,"b":175.25,"text":"Keep the original file, and record every change.","w":[172.24,172.46,172.6,173.04,173.84,173.96,174.52,174.78]},{"s":7,"a":175.55,"b":178.71,"text":"Top tip: look at raw data before any analysis.","w":[175.56,175.88,176.56,176.78,176.9,177.14,177.4,177.78,177.98]},{"s":7,"a":179.01,"b":181.6,"text":"Knowzone is here whenever you want to practise.","w":[179.1,179.66,179.8,180.16,180.54,180.68,180.86,180.98]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"Garbage in","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Confident survey answer felt wrong?"},{"at":4.4,"kind":"text","text":"Today: collect data fairly; clean it before trusting it"}]},{"at":12.2,"heading":"Collecting data","items":[{"at":12.35,"kind":"text","text":"Garbage in, garbage out"},{"at":18.97,"kind":"term","text":"Population","detail":"Everyone/everything you want to know about"},{"at":18.97,"kind":"term","text":"Sample","detail":"Part you actually measure"},{"at":24.99,"kind":"term","text":"Representative","detail":"Reflects the whole population; choosing at random helps"},{"at":31.22,"kind":"text","text":"Biased sample: wrong answers however big"}]},{"at":34.6,"heading":"Sampling pitfalls","items":[{"at":34.75,"kind":"text","text":"Football-match sample"},{"at":38.62,"kind":"text","text":"Not the nation's view"},{"at":40.76,"kind":"text","text":"Larger random samples → steadier results"},{"at":40.76,"kind":"text","text":"Clear, neutral questions; record units"}]},{"at":47.24,"heading":"Cleaning data","items":[{"at":47.39,"kind":"text","text":"Large share of data scientists' time"},{"at":51.21,"kind":"text","text":"Missing values: leave out/fill carefully; state choice"},{"at":58.95,"kind":"term","text":"Duplicates","detail":"Same record entered twice"},{"at":62.97,"kind":"text","text":"Fix formats/spellings: Lagos = lagos = LAGOS"}]},{"at":70.89,"heading":"More cleaning checks","items":[{"at":71.04,"kind":"text","text":"Dates: different orders; units mixed (m, cm)"},{"at":76.57,"kind":"text","text":"Impossible values/typing errors: age 200"},{"at":80.81,"kind":"text","text":"Outliers: check mistake or real before removing"},{"at":85.81,"kind":"text","text":"Keep original file untouched; record every change"}]},{"at":90.44,"heading":"Worked example","items":[{"at":93.19,"kind":"text","text":"Duplicate row → remove"},{"at":98.22,"kind":"text","text":"Missing age → leave out/fill; state choice"},{"at":104.24,"kind":"text","text":"Lagos/lagos/LAGOS → one spelling"},{"at":110.63,"kind":"formula","text":"170 cm = 1.7 m"},{"at":118.39,"kind":"text","text":"Keep original; record every change"}]},{"at":122.78,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":122.78,"kind":"question","text":"A survey about internet use is carried out only online. What is wrong with the sample?"}]},{"at":132.41,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":132.56,"kind":"text","text":"Online-only sample"},{"at":132.56,"kind":"text","text":"Leaves out rarely/never online → biased"}]},{"at":137.56,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":137.71,"kind":"wrong","text":"Analyse before inspecting raw data"},{"at":144.89,"kind":"wrong","text":"Delete outliers unchecked; guess missing values silently"},{"at":153.2,"kind":"wrong","text":"Big sample cannot be biased"}]},{"at":159.7,"heading":"Recap","items":[{"at":159.85,"kind":"text","text":"Representative random sample; clear neutral questions"},{"at":165.05,"kind":"text","text":"Clean: missing, duplicates, formats, impossible, outliers"},{"at":172.13,"kind":"text","text":"Keep original; record every change"},{"at":175.45,"kind":"tip","text":"Look at raw data before any analysis"},{"at":178.91,"kind":"text","text":"Knowzone: practise anytime"}]}],"check":{"at":132.06,"seconds":10,"question":"A survey about internet use is carried out only online. What is wrong with the sample?","answer":"It leaves out people who are rarely or never online, so it is biased."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}